  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Why linear output alone is insufficient:** We need outputs in $[0, 1]$ to interpret them as probabilities. A linear function is unbounded. We need a **squashing** function."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "# Section 3: Sigmoid Activation\n",
    "\n",
    "## The Sigmoid Function\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\sigma(z) = \\frac{1}{1 + e^{-z}} = \\frac{e^z}{1 + e^z}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Properties:\n",
    "- Maps $(-\\infty, +\\infty) \\to (0, 1)$\n",
    "- $\\sigma(0) = 0.5$\n",
    "- $\\sigma(z) \\to 1$ as $z \\to +\\infty$\n",
    "- $\\sigma(z) \\to 0$ as $z \\to -\\infty$\n",
    "\n",
    "**Saturation problem:** When $|z|$ is large, the curve flattens (saturates). Gradients become tiny, slowing learning."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 36,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
