    "## What If We Classify Without Sigmoid?\n",
    "\n",
    "If we threshold the **raw linear output** directly (e.g., predict 1 if $z > 0$), we get a valid decision boundary. But:\n",
    "- We lose probabilistic interpretation\n",
    "- The gradient of a step function is 0 almost everywhere → no gradient signal for learning!\n",
    "- Sigmoid gives smooth gradients that drive learning"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 39,
